compared with US$95.3 million and US$103.2 million as of June 30, 2025 and March 31, 2026.</FONT> The cash balance increase was primarily
driven by enhanced working capital efficiency, which more than offset the net loss recorded during the period.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"></P>

